  "$brand": "The mark's geometry, as ratios of its own font size, so `|Stint|` is one drawing rather than a web one and a Swift one that resemble each other. It lived in both `wordmark.tsx` and `Mark.swift` and had already diverged — the bounds were 1.05em on the web and cap height on macOS, a difference nobody chose. Ratios rather than pixels because the mark is set at 17px in a panel header and 24px in the app header off the same definition. Colour is deliberately absent: the mark takes ONE colour including its bounds, so it inherits `currentColor` and has nothing to parameterise.",
  "brand": {
    "mark": {
      "boundWidth": 0.09,
      "boundHeight": 1.05,
      "boundGap": 0.18,
      "boundRadius": 999
    }
  },

  "$elevation": "Composite shadow values, not colours, so they live outside `semantic` and pass through the generator untouched. Theme-aware: a dark ground needs a near-opaque shadow to read at all, a light one needs a much softer alpha or it looks like soot.",
  "elevation": {
    "dark": {
      "shadow-card":  "0 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,0.40), 0 2px 10px rgba(0,0,0,0.34)",
      "shadow-float": "0 2px 4px rgba(0,0,0,0.44), 0 8px 24px rgba(0,0,0,0.40)"
    },
    "light": {
      "shadow-card":  "0 1px 2px rgba(16,18,26,0.06), 0 2px 8px rgba(16,18,26,0.07)",
      "shadow-float": "0 2px 4px rgba(16,18,26,0.08), 0 8px 24px rgba(16,18,26,0.10)"
    }
  },

